.TH users 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
users \- print the user names of users currently logged in to the current host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY users
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Output who is currently logged in according to FILE.
If FILE is not specified, use \fI\,/var/run/utmp\/\fP.  \fI\,/var/log/wtmp\/\fP as FILE is common.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/users#users\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/users#users\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Joseph Arceneaux and David MacKenzie.
